{# The totals box a sell-side document's create/edit screen shows below its line-items table —
   Subtotal, before-tax fees, tax lines, Total Tax, after-tax fees, Grand Total, each with a
   js-{hookPrefix}-total-* class so app.js's recalc functions can update it live as the admin
   edits. Built from Order's own totals box (`order/form.html.twig`), shared outward per the
   owner's ruling 2026-09-13: "apply the common shared blocks, and where there is differences,
   add/adjust for exceptions. NOT start with different template and find shared blocks."

   Order's box is ALWAYS this one structure — the same markup whether the document is brand new
   (figures start at $0.00/blank) or already exists (figures start at their stored value): the JS
   hook classes are present either way, and recalcOrderTotals() keeps them current as lines and
   charges change, with the server figure as the honest starting point. Invoice's own "Computed on
   save" placeholder is replaced by rendering through this same file, computing a real starting
   figure the identical way.

   Quote is wired through this file too (#full-parity, 2026-09-13: "Quote total box should just be
   the same as SO" — default is the shared structure, exceptions are raised as needed, not assumed).
   Its one real difference is the TBD business rule (#254 — a quote may be saved before every line
   is priced or shipping is resolved): any of the three display parameters below may be the literal
   string 'TBD' instead of a number, which prints as-is with no leading $. Order and Invoice never
   pass that, so nothing changes for them. Quote folds shipping into the same single Subtotal figure
   Order does — there is no separate Shipping row — so the honest answer while shipping is still
   unresolved is the same 'TBD' on Subtotal that an unpriced line already puts there.

   What is NOT shared here either way: the CHARGE-ROW EDITORS (the shipping/tax/fee rows an admin
   types into). Different documents bind different JS container classes to them for live
   client-side insertion, so moving those into this file would require rewriting that wiring —
   out of scope for a totals-DISPLAY unification. Each caller renders its own charge-row editors
   and hands the finished markup in through the three slots below.

   Parameters
   ----------
   hookPrefix           required  'order' | 'invoice' | 'estimate' — used for every
                                   js-{hookPrefix}-total-* class, so app.js's own recalc functions
                                   keep finding them.
   subtotalDisplay      required  pre-formatted string, e.g. "130.50" or "0.00" (no $ — the
                                   template adds it), or the literal string 'TBD'.
   beforeTaxFeeLines    optional  list of {label, amount} shown between Subtotal and the tax lines
                                   — main-line fees not already folded into Subtotal.
   taxLines             optional  list of {label, rate, amount} — the document's own tax breakdown.
   taxLinesTotalDisplay required  pre-formatted string (no $), or 'TBD', for "Total Tax".
   afterTaxFeeLines     optional  list of {label, amount} shown after Total Tax, before Grand Total.
   grandTotalDisplay    required  pre-formatted string (no $), or 'TBD', for "Grand Total".
   beforeSubtotalSlot   optional  pre-rendered HTML (marked |raw by the caller) for charge-row
                                   editors that belong ABOVE Subtotal (shipping + main-line fees).
   afterTaxFeeSlot      optional  pre-rendered HTML for after-tax-fee charge-row editors, kept
                                   separate so they land where their own total line does.
   taxSlot              optional  pre-rendered HTML for tax-type charge-row editors.
   pendingSlot          optional  pre-rendered HTML shown right after Subtotal — Quote's own
                                   "Lines not yet priced" counter, which Order and Invoice have no
                                   use for and so never pass.
   afterGrandTotalSlot  optional  pre-rendered HTML shown after Grand Total — Invoice's own Payment
                                   and Owed Balance rows (#full-parity, 2026-09-13), which Order and
                                   Quote have no use for and so never pass.
#}
{% macro totals_footer(hookPrefix, subtotalDisplay, beforeTaxFeeLines, taxLines, taxLinesTotalDisplay, afterTaxFeeLines, grandTotalDisplay, beforeSubtotalSlot, afterTaxFeeSlot, taxSlot, pendingSlot, afterGrandTotalSlot) %}
    <div class="order-total-box">
        {% if beforeSubtotalSlot is not empty %}{{ beforeSubtotalSlot|raw }}{% endif %}
        <div><span>Subtotal:</span><strong class="js-{{ hookPrefix }}-total-before-tax">{{ subtotalDisplay == 'TBD' ? 'TBD' : '$' ~ subtotalDisplay }}</strong></div>
        {% if pendingSlot is not empty %}{{ pendingSlot|raw }}{% endif %}
        {% set _taxLinesWrapClass = 'js-' ~ hookPrefix ~ '-tax-lines-wrap' %}
        <div class="{{ _taxLinesWrapClass }}" style="display:contents;">
            {% for feeLine in beforeTaxFeeLines|default([]) %}
                <div><span>{{ feeLine.label }}:</span><strong>${{ feeLine.amount|amount }}</strong></div>
            {% endfor %}
            {% for taxLine in taxLines|default([]) %}
                <div><span>{{ taxLine.label }}{% if taxLine.rate is not null %} {{ (taxLine.rate * 100)|number_format(0) }}%{% endif %}:</span><strong>${{ taxLine.amount|amount }}</strong></div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <div><span>Total Tax:</span><strong class="js-{{ hookPrefix }}-total-tax">{{ taxLinesTotalDisplay == 'TBD' ? 'TBD' : '$' ~ taxLinesTotalDisplay }}</strong></div>
        {% for feeLine in afterTaxFeeLines|default([]) %}
            <div><span>{{ feeLine.label }}:</span><strong>${{ feeLine.amount|amount }}</strong></div>
        {% endfor %}
        {% if afterTaxFeeSlot is not empty %}{{ afterTaxFeeSlot|raw }}{% endif %}
        {% if taxSlot is not empty %}{{ taxSlot|raw }}{% endif %}
        <div><span>Grand Total:</span><strong class="js-{{ hookPrefix }}-total-grand">{{ grandTotalDisplay == 'TBD' ? 'TBD' : '$' ~ grandTotalDisplay }}</strong></div>
        {% if afterGrandTotalSlot is not empty %}{{ afterGrandTotalSlot|raw }}{% endif %}
    </div>
{% endmacro %}
